\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Wiring diagram of the electronic components. The battery and breadboard are used to power the Arduino UNO and L298N motor driver. UNO communicates with MPU-6050 inertial measurement unit (IMU) using I2C protocol, and sends analog signal to the motor driver using pulse width modulation (PWM). The motor driver controls 2 motors.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:wire_diagram}{{2}{2}{Wiring diagram of the electronic components. The battery and breadboard are used to power the Arduino UNO and L298N motor driver. UNO communicates with MPU-6050 inertial measurement unit (IMU) using I2C protocol, and sends analog signal to the motor driver using pulse width modulation (PWM). The motor driver controls 2 motors}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:wire_diagram@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][1][]2}{}{}{}}
